@ralienpp there was an implicit choice made to not scrub, AV scan, or try to analyze submitted files as they are loaded in the platform. There are tools for scrubbing metadata that are well made and shipped by default with Tails. There are many good reasons for keeping the interaction of core software small with formats that are notorious for providing RCEs. Further Globaleaks has a data retention policy that by default removes submitted data within 15 days

For setups that use PGP the content of the files is stored encrypted on the server. If PGP is not encrypted the Whistleblower is informed in the interface that their intended recipients are not encrypting files. That warning might not quiet address the meta data issue and could be changed to include language about the risk of Personally Identifiable Information/Metadata.

This --> FAQS
